Rebased, and pushed two more commits, WDYT @lyrixx?

1. `#[Place]` on a class constant is now read (it was silently ignored), a bare `#[AsGuardListener]` in the class now guards its own workflow instead of every workflow of the app, and there's one way to declare things: `transitions:`, the list form of `places:`, `Transition::$name` and `Place::$name` are gone, and `Arc` stays as is since `new Arc(Status::Approved->value, 2)` works in attributes. This commit also covers your comments @stof, including a state machine `#[Transition]` with several places now throwing instead of being split.
2. The attributes now go through the `workflow` config tree instead of being validated a second time, which removes the descriptors. The config now also accepts workflows with neither `supports` nor `support_strategy`, like the attributes did.
